  RESIDUAL  #
  RESIDUAL  # leglo(w,r) = w -. r,  leghi(w,r) = w + r,  splitnorm(w,r) = w*w -. r*r
  RESIDUAL  # over N with truncated subtraction (PairVocab section 3c / section 10).
  RESIDUAL  #
  RESIDUAL  # THE TARGET, first line: the split norm identity, the one of
  RESIDUAL  # PairCoordinates.agda three ring identities that survives truncation.
  RESIDUAL  # NEGATIVE CONTROLS.  Both are TRUE over Z (PairCoordinates.agda proves
  RESIDUAL  # them over any commutative ring) and FALSE over N off the cone r <= w.
  RESIDUAL  # They must be dropped by the fingerprint filter BEFORE any proof attempt;
  RESIDUAL  # if either ever reaches the prover this seed file is lying.
  RESIDUAL  # WHY LINE 1 IS STILL OPEN, and it is not the vocabulary.
  RESIDUAL  #
  RESIDUAL  # leglo(x,y)*leghi(x,y) = splitnorm(x,y) -- i.e. (x -. y)*(x + y) = x*x -. y*y
  RESIDUAL  # over N -- reaches the prover on every run and comes back attempted-no-proof,
  RESIDUAL  # including at --nested-depth 3.  The reason is structural and is in monus, not
  RESIDUAL  # in the pair chart:
  RESIDUAL  #
  RESIDUAL  #   `-` is the only symbol in this vocabulary whose defining equations recurse
  RESIDUAL  #   on BOTH arguments at once (MathMachine.hs baseVocabulary: -(x,0) = x,
  RESIDUAL  #   -(0,x) = 0, -(s x, s y) = -(x,y)).  proveByInduction (MathMachine.hs
  RESIDUAL  #   ~1280) substitutes s# for exactly ONE variable in the step case, so in a
  RESIDUAL  #   step case built from a two-variable monus term the other argument is still
  RESIDUAL  #   a bare variable and NO monus clause can fire.  Induction on x leaves
  RESIDUAL  #   -(s#, y); induction on y leaves -(x, s#); both are irreducible.  Nested
  RESIDUAL  #   induction does not help, because the inner induction inherits the same
  RESIDUAL  #   one-variable substitution.
  RESIDUAL  #
  RESIDUAL  # So the split norm needs either a prover that splits a PAIR of variables into
  RESIDUAL  # (0,y) / (x,0) / (s x, s y), or a lemma chain that removes the two-variable
  RESIDUAL  # monus first -- the natural one is right-distributivity (x -. y)*z =
  RESIDUAL  # x*z -. y*z together with cancellation (a + c) -. (c + b) = a -. b, and the
  RESIDUAL  # first of those is blocked by the identical obstruction.  That is the next
  RESIDUAL  # piece of work, and it is a prover, not a vocabulary.
